            <ArticleTitle>Aneurysm of a saphenous vein bypass graft associated with aneurysms of native coronary arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>489-94</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aneurysm formation in saphenous vein aortocoronary bypass grafts is an extremely rare complication of coronary artery bypass surgery. Aneurysms of native coronary arteries are found in a small percentage of patients at autopsy. Reported is a case with multiple coronary artery aneurysms in which a dissecting aneurysm of the saphenous vein bypass graft also developed following coronary artery bypass surgery. This is the first report of such association.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
